    {
      "schema_version": 6,
      "book_id": "NAM",
      "chapter": 3,
      "chapter_usfm": "NAM.3",
      "version_id": 90,
      "version_abbr": "LEB",
      "verses": [
        {
          "verse": 1,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.1",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Woe to the city that has shed much blood! She is a deceiver, She is filled with plunder, She has hoarded her spoils of war."
        },
        {
          "verse": 2,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.2",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "The crack of the whip! The rumbling of the chariot wheel! The galloping of the horse! The racing of the chariot!"
        },
        {
          "verse": 3,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.3",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Chariots charge! Swords flash! Spears glitter! Many corpses are piled high! There is no end to the slain! They stumble over their dead!"
        },
        {
          "verse": 4,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.4",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "“Because of the many idolatries of the prostitute, the beautiful charm of a mistress of witchcraft, she who enslaves nations by her harlotries, and peoples by her sorceries,"
        },
        {
          "verse": 5,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.5",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "“Look! I am against you!” declaresYahweh. “I will strip up your skirts over your face; I will let nations look at your nakedness and your shame."
        },
        {
          "verse": 6,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.6",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "“I will throw filth upon you, I will treat you with contempt, I will make you a spectacle."
        },
        {
          "verse": 7,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.7",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "“And it will be that everyone who sees you will flee from you, And they will say, ‘Nineveh is destroyed!’ Who will mourn for her? From whence shall I seek comforters for you?”"
        },
        {
          "verse": 8,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.8",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Are you better than Thebes? She who sits at the Nile, surrounded by her waters, her rampart was the sea and water was her wall."
        },
        {
          "verse": 9,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.9",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Cush was her strength, Egypt without end; Put and Libya were among your allies."
        },
        {
          "verse": 10,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.10",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Yet she went into captivity as an exile; her children were dashed to pieces at the head of the streets; they cast lots for all of her nobles; all of her dignitaries were bound with chains."
        },
        {
          "verse": 11,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.11",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "You also will behave like a drunkard; You also will hide yourself; You also will seek refuge from the enemy."
        },
        {
          "verse": 12,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.12",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "All of your fortifications are like fig trees with ripe firstfruits— if they are shaken, they will fall into the mouth of the eater."
        },
        {
          "verse": 13,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.13",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Look! Your troops are like women in your midst. The gates of your land are wide open to your enemies; fire will consume the bars of your gates."
        },
        {
          "verse": 14,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.14",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Draw water for a siege! Strengthen your fortifications! Go to the mud pit! Trample the clay! Grasp the brick mold!"
        },
        {
          "verse": 15,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.15",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "There fire will consume you; the sword will cut you off. It will consume you like the locust. Multiply yourself like the locust! Multiply yourself like the grasshopper!"
        },
        {
          "verse": 16,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.16",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "You have increased your merchants more than the stars of heaven; like the locust they will shed their skin and fly away."
        },
        {
          "verse": 17,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.17",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Your officials are like locusts; your commanders are like a swarm of locusts. They encamp on the walls on a cold day; when the sun rises, they fly away— no one knows where they have gone."
        },
        {
          "verse": 18,
          "usfm": "NAM.3.18",
          "line_type": null,
          "text": "Your shepherds are sleeping, O king of Assyria! Your nobles slumber. Your people are scattered on the mountains; no one can gather them."
        },
        {
          "verse": 19,
